    "body": "In the Electrek Podcast , we discuss the most popular news in the world of sustainable transport and energy. In this week’s episode, we’ll discuss Tesla launching the ‘personal’ Cybercab, Ford’s LFP for Fathom, Aptera delivering, and more.\nThe show is live every Friday at 4 p.m. ET on Electrek ’s YouTube channel .\nAs a reminder, we’ll have an accompanying post, like this one, on the site with an embedded link to the live stream. Head to the YouTube channel to get your questions and comments in.\nAfter the show ends at around 5 p.m. ET, the video will be archived on YouTube and the audio on all your favorite podcast apps:\nAdvertisement - scroll for more content\nApple Podcasts\nSpotify\nOvercast\nPocket Casts\nCastro\nRSS\nWe now have a Patreon if you want to help us avoid more ads and invest more in our content. We have some awesome gifts for our Patreons and more coming.\nHere are a few of the articles that we will discuss during the podcast:\nTesla Cybercab’s autonomy agreement is insane: $299/mo or it doesn’t move\nElon Musk announces another Tesla vehicle no one asked for\nTesla confirms €3B Cybercab factory at Giga Berlin for up to 1M a year\nTesla unveils 7.4 MW Powercore to take on ex-exec Baglino’s Heron Link\nTesla toughens FSD driver monitoring in Europe while loosening it in the US\nWaymo halts highway operation nationwide after CA DMV pause\nFord’s first LFP batteries are en route, and the $30,000 Fathom EV pickup will get them first\nAptera (SEV) completes its first customer solar EV — for its top crowdfunder\nBYD’s folding steering wheel isn’t a concept — it’s in a $49K SUV now\nScout Motors starts validation builds at $2B SC plant, deliveries in 2028\nHere’s the live stream for today’s episode starting at 4:00 p.m. ET (or the video after 5 p.m. ET):\nFTC: We use income earning auto affiliate links. More.\nStay up to date with the latest content by subscribing to Electrek on Google News . You’re reading Electrek— experts who break news about Tesla , electric vehicles, and green energy , day after day. Be sure to check out our homepage for all the latest news, and follow Electrek on X , Facebook , and LinkedIn to stay in the loop. Don’t know where to start? Check out our YouTube channel for the latest reviews.",
